1
00:01:42,159 --> 00:01:43,439
So during this operation,

2
00:01:43,439 --> 00:01:45,239
there are four factions we need to watch out for.

3
00:01:45,599 --> 00:01:48,719
First are the primitive tribes in the remote mountains.

4
00:01:48,879 --> 00:01:51,239
Second are the terrorists.

5
00:01:51,519 --> 00:01:54,040
Third are rogue bandit gangs.

6
00:01:54,239 --> 00:01:55,040
And fourth,

7
00:01:55,439 --> 00:01:57,480
the guards who betrayed Marisa to the terrorists.

8
00:01:58,239 --> 00:02:00,959
What matters most, however, are these four engineers.

9
00:02:01,239 --> 00:02:03,760
On the route between the hotel and the site,

10
00:02:04,040 --> 00:02:06,239
as well as during their work there,

11
00:02:06,439 --> 00:02:08,680
we may need colleagues from Bito Group

12
00:02:08,680 --> 00:02:10,479
to provide armed perimeter security.

13
00:02:10,520 --> 00:02:11,680
That won't be a problem.

14
00:02:12,400 --> 00:02:14,879
We're partners now.

15
00:02:15,199 --> 00:02:16,840
We'll treat Zhong An's mission

16
00:02:16,840 --> 00:02:18,759
just like our own.

17
00:02:20,719 --> 00:02:21,520
Marisa.

18
00:02:22,319 --> 00:02:24,360
Don't sit by the window. Sit over there.

19
00:02:25,400 --> 00:02:26,199
It's dangerous.

20
00:02:27,560 --> 00:02:29,280
You're paranoid all day long.

21
00:02:30,039 --> 00:02:31,319
Is it really that serious?

22
00:02:32,639 --> 00:02:33,599
You're always like this.

23
00:02:34,319 --> 00:02:35,719
No matter what happens,

24
00:02:36,240 --> 00:02:39,000
you always stay so calm.

25
00:02:39,599 --> 00:02:41,639
Really? I don't think so.

26
00:02:42,280 --> 00:02:44,039
I remember always being sharp and decisive.

27
00:02:45,360 --> 00:02:48,560
I recall you catching a snake to cook,

28
00:02:48,560 --> 00:02:50,080
and spending the entire afternoon on it.

29
00:02:51,080 --> 00:02:51,879
Wei Tian.

30
00:02:52,319 --> 00:02:55,439
I remember you loved astronomy back then,

31
00:02:55,639 --> 00:02:57,919
stargazing all day and night.

32
00:02:59,319 --> 00:03:00,120
Yeah.

33
00:03:01,080 --> 00:03:01,879
Back then,

34
00:03:03,400 --> 00:03:07,280
I loved stargazing and hunting.

35
00:03:08,240 --> 00:03:11,800
I'd sleep so soundly I wouldn't even dream.

36
00:03:11,919 --> 00:03:13,199
Let's go hunting another day, then.

37
00:03:13,360 --> 00:03:13,800
Sure.

38
00:03:14,159 --> 00:03:15,960
We'll go once our job is finished.

39
00:03:18,919 --> 00:03:20,280
Ma'am, Anda is here.

40
00:03:22,319 --> 00:03:24,719
Hello, ma'am. Did you send for me?

41
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:25,879
Miss Anda,

42
00:03:26,319 --> 00:03:27,759
I have a shopping list here.

43
00:03:27,759 --> 00:03:29,120
Could you pick these up for me?

44
00:03:37,840 --> 00:03:40,439
What do you need these for?

45
00:03:41,159 --> 00:03:43,000
A grand hotel like the Plato...

46
00:03:43,039 --> 00:03:44,960
surely has these items, right?

47
00:03:47,560 --> 00:03:48,360
Impossible.

48
00:03:49,680 --> 00:03:51,120
Do you have any other questions, then?

49
00:03:51,919 --> 00:03:52,719
None at all.

50
00:03:53,039 --> 00:03:54,560
I'll go buy them for you right away.

51
00:03:59,599 --> 00:04:01,240
This girl is quite something.

52
00:04:03,199 --> 00:04:04,840
Just eat your snacks.

53
00:04:08,159 --> 00:04:08,960
Yang Di, Yang Di!

54
00:04:09,759 --> 00:04:11,560
Hey, could you take a look at this?

55
00:04:11,560 --> 00:04:13,159
Where can I buy these things?

56
00:04:13,479 --> 00:04:14,280
What are they?

57
00:04:16,240 --> 00:04:17,600
Who asked you to buy this stuff?

58
00:04:18,720 --> 00:04:21,000
Who else? Her, of course.

59
00:04:21,600 --> 00:04:24,560
Roses, vanilla, essential oils...

60
00:04:24,560 --> 00:04:26,560
stars, perfume, needles...

61
00:04:26,720 --> 00:04:28,279
What do you think these are for?

62
00:04:28,480 --> 00:04:31,399
It's not like this is a trendy place.

63
00:04:31,399 --> 00:04:33,360
Asking for all this is clearly messing with me.

64
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:36,240
Anda, let me tell you something.

65
00:04:36,399 --> 00:04:38,720
These might look like fashionable items,

66
00:04:39,160 --> 00:04:41,920
but they clash with local customs.

67
00:04:42,519 --> 00:04:44,759
Take roses, for example.

68
00:04:44,759 --> 00:04:46,319
What do you think they mean?

69
00:04:47,360 --> 00:04:49,079
They stand for love everywhere.

70
00:04:49,079 --> 00:04:49,720
Wrong.

71
00:04:50,040 --> 00:04:52,439
Here, roses are used for mourning.

72
00:04:52,439 --> 00:04:53,360
And those stars...

73
00:04:53,360 --> 00:04:54,360
you can't just use them casually here either.

74
00:04:54,480 --> 00:04:55,600
Especially these needles.

75
00:04:55,600 --> 00:04:56,920
They're considered very bad luck.

76
00:04:58,639 --> 00:05:00,920
Be careful. Don't say I didn't warn you.

77
00:05:01,319 --> 00:05:02,879
Then why did she ask me to buy them?

78
00:05:03,399 --> 00:05:04,439
Who knows?

79
00:05:04,439 --> 00:05:06,319
You probably offended her.

80
00:05:08,399 --> 00:05:09,759
Is it because of Wei Tian?

81
00:05:14,120 --> 00:05:14,920
Is it?

82
00:05:15,439 --> 00:05:16,439
Definitely.

83
00:05:19,399 --> 00:05:21,680
There's something I don't quite get.

84
00:05:22,439 --> 00:05:23,680
We've already got everything

85
00:05:23,680 --> 00:05:24,959
completely prepared.

86
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:26,319
Why does Marisa

87
00:05:26,439 --> 00:05:27,360
still refuse to allow our

88
00:05:27,360 --> 00:05:28,720
VIPs onto the construction site?

89
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:32,399
Lately, I've also felt

90
00:05:33,879 --> 00:05:36,079
it's been unusually quiet.

91
00:05:36,240 --> 00:05:37,040
Quiet?

92
00:05:38,959 --> 00:05:41,360
The calm before the storm?

93
00:05:41,720 --> 00:05:43,839
Not bad, kid. You're learning.

94
00:05:46,160 --> 00:05:47,439
In our line of work,

95
00:05:48,240 --> 00:05:50,759
you have to be as sharp as an eagle

96
00:05:50,879 --> 00:05:52,240
and nip trouble in the bud.

97
00:05:53,360 --> 00:05:54,120
Over the next few days,

98
00:05:54,120 --> 00:05:56,319
we must tighten hotel security.

99
00:05:56,680 --> 00:05:57,480
Understood.

100
00:05:57,560 --> 00:05:58,439
You really get it?

101
00:05:58,759 --> 00:05:59,560
I really do.

102
00:06:38,759 --> 00:06:40,079
Anda's been gone for so long.

103
00:06:40,079 --> 00:06:41,240
Why isn't she back yet?

104
00:06:41,759 --> 00:06:43,519
Could it be that while buying things for me,

105
00:06:44,199 --> 00:06:45,240
something happened to her?

106
00:06:50,279 --> 00:06:52,120
Stay put. I'll go check.

107
00:07:04,879 --> 00:07:06,040
You're always chasing things

108
00:07:06,040 --> 00:07:07,120
you can never catch.

109
00:07:07,120 --> 00:07:07,759
Who's there?

110
00:07:07,879 --> 00:07:09,439
I'm a gentleman.

111
00:07:09,480 --> 00:07:11,399
You're about to receive a gift.

112
00:08:35,879 --> 00:08:37,039
You can't go outside right now.

113
00:08:37,080 --> 00:08:38,240
It's too dangerous out there.

114
00:08:38,360 --> 00:08:39,919
I've seen this plenty of times.

115
00:08:40,000 --> 00:08:41,080
In my dictionary,

116
00:08:41,080 --> 00:08:42,440
the concept of danger doesn't exist.

117
00:08:42,480 --> 00:08:43,919
You're our client right now,

118
00:08:43,919 --> 00:08:45,440
and it's my duty to keep you safe.

119
00:09:05,879 --> 00:09:06,679
Fall back to the hotel!

120
00:09:06,679 --> 00:09:07,440
Yes, sir!

121
00:09:08,120 --> 00:09:08,919
Move!

122
00:09:09,159 --> 00:09:09,960
Move, move, move!

123
00:09:10,960 --> 00:09:11,759
Let's go!

124
00:09:15,080 --> 00:09:15,399
Go!

125
00:09:15,399 --> 00:09:15,840
Hurry!

126
00:09:25,879 --> 00:09:27,200
Their fire's too heavy!

127
00:09:27,200 --> 00:09:28,360
Find a fire hydrant, quick!

128
00:09:28,360 --> 00:09:28,799
Got it!

129
00:09:47,240 --> 00:09:48,039
Take this.

130
00:10:27,720 --> 00:10:28,840
Thanks to you guys this time.

131
00:10:29,120 --> 00:10:29,960
Thank you so much.

132
00:10:30,320 --> 00:10:31,759
Now's not the time for this.

133
00:10:31,919 --> 00:10:33,720
Settle them in and wait for Wei Tian to get back.

134
00:10:33,720 --> 00:10:35,480
Okay, I'll head back to the hotel first.

135
00:10:35,519 --> 00:10:36,720
We'll meet at the hotel later.

136
00:10:38,200 --> 00:10:39,000
Wait a second.

137
00:10:40,120 --> 00:10:41,399
Whatever you do, don't rush outside.

138
00:10:41,480 --> 00:10:42,840
You must wait until Wei Tian gets back.

139
00:10:43,039 --> 00:10:43,600
Got it.

140
00:10:45,360 --> 00:10:45,759
Let's go.

141
00:10:46,120 --> 00:10:46,879
Wei Tian.

142
00:10:46,879 --> 00:10:48,559
The hotel was just hit by an armed attack.

143
00:10:48,559 --> 00:10:49,720
The VIPs are safe for now.

144
00:10:49,759 --> 00:10:50,559
Where are you?

145
00:10:50,759 --> 00:10:52,200
Anda's been kidnapped.

146
00:10:52,200 --> 00:10:54,159
I'm heading to the kidnappers' location.

147
00:10:54,360 --> 00:10:55,799
Don't leave the hotel right now.

148
00:10:55,960 --> 00:10:56,759
Wait until I get back.

149
00:10:56,759 --> 00:10:58,720
Who on earth is this Hades?

150
00:11:03,120 --> 00:11:04,679
He used to be just like me.

151
00:11:06,039 --> 00:11:07,440
He belonged to Deep Sea.

152
00:11:08,919 --> 00:11:10,759
Later, he betrayed us.

153
00:11:11,679 --> 00:11:14,960
He's the top black market arms dealer now.

154
00:11:16,399 --> 00:11:17,200
What about you?

155
00:11:17,320 --> 00:11:18,120
Me?

156
00:11:20,440 --> 00:11:24,519
Rossi and I are kind of the same.

157
00:11:26,559 --> 00:11:29,320
She traveled abroad with her boyfriend,

158
00:11:30,200 --> 00:11:31,519
and ran into a terrorist attack.

159
00:11:32,240 --> 00:11:33,279
Her boyfriend died.

160
00:11:34,960 --> 00:11:37,559
She... had partial amnesia.

161
00:11:38,159 --> 00:11:41,200
She still hasn't recovered to this day.

162
00:11:43,000 --> 00:11:44,799
Maybe forgetting isn't a bad thing.

163
00:11:46,279 --> 00:11:48,240
We all have our own past.

164
00:11:48,960 --> 00:11:49,759
As long as we don't dwell

165
00:11:49,759 --> 00:11:51,320
on our past, it's fine.

166
00:11:52,919 --> 00:11:54,120
Back when I was in the army,

167
00:11:54,840 --> 00:11:56,000
the instructor told us

168
00:11:56,759 --> 00:11:59,120
every moment is the present.

169
00:11:59,960 --> 00:12:01,120
The moment you throw a punch,

170
00:12:01,840 --> 00:12:03,159
the moment you fire a shot.

171
00:12:04,480 --> 00:12:06,039
Because the very next moment,

172
00:12:06,240 --> 00:12:07,559
we might face death.

173
00:12:11,720 --> 00:12:13,519
Death doesn't matter.

174
00:12:14,000 --> 00:12:15,600
Everyone has to face it.

175
00:12:15,840 --> 00:12:16,840
What matters most is

176
00:12:17,399 --> 00:12:19,440
never dragging your friends down.

177
00:12:21,799 --> 00:12:23,720
So you'd better trust the people around you.

178
00:12:24,440 --> 00:12:25,240
Like me.

179
00:12:38,559 --> 00:12:39,360
Captain.

180
00:12:40,039 --> 00:12:40,840
What happened?

181
00:12:41,360 --> 00:12:42,480
Thomas is dead.

182
00:12:43,240 --> 00:12:45,879
He died, yet here you are.

183
00:12:45,879 --> 00:12:46,679
No, that's not it!

184
00:12:47,639 --> 00:12:49,480
Do you remember before you left,

185
00:12:49,679 --> 00:12:50,919
what you said?

186
00:12:51,080 --> 00:12:53,639
"I won't return until the mission is done."

187
00:12:58,559 --> 00:12:59,960
Please give me another chance.

188
00:13:00,080 --> 00:13:02,240
I'll redeem myself!

189
00:13:02,960 --> 00:13:04,559
If everyone was like you,

190
00:13:04,559 --> 00:13:05,600
failing their mission

191
00:13:05,600 --> 00:13:07,559
and standing here without a scratch,

192
00:13:07,799 --> 00:13:10,720
who would still put their life on the line?

193
00:13:11,200 --> 00:13:14,240
I promise, I promise I'll get it done this time!

194
00:13:14,919 --> 00:13:16,120
Just give me one more chance!

195
00:13:16,559 --> 00:13:17,960
Captain! Captain!

196
00:13:18,840 --> 00:13:21,000
Trust me, I can finish it!

197
00:13:23,000 --> 00:13:24,960
Captain, please!

198
00:13:48,559 --> 00:13:49,559
We can't get any closer.

199
00:14:21,039 --> 00:14:21,840
Morris.

200
00:14:26,240 --> 00:14:27,840
Rip the tape off her mouth.

201
00:14:38,919 --> 00:14:41,480
Seems Wei Tian's taste has changed quite a bit.

202
00:14:42,960 --> 00:14:44,120
Why did you kidnap me?

203
00:14:44,279 --> 00:14:45,360
I... If you want money,

204
00:14:45,360 --> 00:14:46,559
no one around me has any!

205
00:14:46,559 --> 00:14:48,080
I... I really don't have any money.

206
00:14:49,559 --> 00:14:51,080
What a coincidence.

207
00:14:51,960 --> 00:14:53,799
How about I help you clear

208
00:14:54,000 --> 00:14:55,200
all your debts this time?

209
00:14:56,879 --> 00:14:57,679
Wait, what...

210
00:14:58,480 --> 00:15:00,000
What do you really want?

211
00:15:00,000 --> 00:15:00,399
I...

212
00:15:00,399 --> 00:15:01,120
What are you doing?

213
00:15:02,600 --> 00:15:04,879
Morris, be polite.

214
00:15:06,399 --> 00:15:09,279
The Wei Tian I know is a generous man.

215
00:15:09,720 --> 00:15:11,799
He'd never stop others from making money,

216
00:15:13,200 --> 00:15:16,600
much less let those close to him get hurt.

217
00:15:17,720 --> 00:15:19,879
What does that have to do with me?

218
00:15:20,039 --> 00:15:20,919
I really have no money.

219
00:15:20,919 --> 00:15:22,759
Nobody I know has any money!

220
00:15:23,039 --> 00:15:23,840
No, no, no.

221
00:15:24,840 --> 00:15:26,639
Why would I want your money?

222
00:15:27,279 --> 00:15:29,679
I invited you here as my guest

223
00:15:30,000 --> 00:15:31,600
so that our mutual friend, Wei Tian,

224
00:15:31,600 --> 00:15:32,559
can drop by for a chat.

225
00:15:33,639 --> 00:15:34,440
Actually,

226
00:15:35,120 --> 00:15:37,320
I can't stand seeing a woman wronged.

227
00:15:37,840 --> 00:15:39,279
Maybe I don't always succeed,

228
00:15:39,720 --> 00:15:41,919
but I do try my best to be a gentleman.

229
00:15:42,840 --> 00:15:43,720
You know...

230
00:15:44,360 --> 00:15:46,200
you have a wonderful trait.

231
00:15:46,440 --> 00:15:47,480
Kindness.

232
00:15:48,279 --> 00:15:49,399
I hope that when our friend

233
00:15:49,399 --> 00:15:50,320
Wei Tian arrives later,

234
00:15:50,320 --> 00:15:51,559
he can be just like you—

235
00:15:51,679 --> 00:15:54,000
kind to others, and kind to himself.

236
00:15:55,519 --> 00:15:58,399
Morris, take good care of our guest.

237
00:16:50,639 --> 00:16:52,559
Watch your surroundings and stay sharp.

238
00:16:52,879 --> 00:16:53,679
Copy that.

239
00:17:09,039 --> 00:17:10,559
Get some good rest after your shift.

240
00:17:10,559 --> 00:17:11,200
Will do.

241
00:17:21,759 --> 00:17:23,880
Freeze! You're surrounded!

242
00:17:44,559 --> 00:17:45,359
Anda.

243
00:17:50,440 --> 00:17:51,559
Hello, Wei Tian.

244
00:17:52,279 --> 00:17:53,359
Long time no see.

245
00:18:00,759 --> 00:18:01,559
Hades.

246
00:18:03,200 --> 00:18:04,720
I knew it was you all along.

247
00:18:06,400 --> 00:18:07,400
Leave my friend alone.

248
00:18:08,000 --> 00:18:08,799
Come at me.

249
00:18:09,279 --> 00:18:11,279
Seems you know the situation quite well.

250
00:18:11,519 --> 00:18:14,759
What do you want this time?

251
00:18:15,880 --> 00:18:17,960
I'm not a soldier anymore.

252
00:18:18,240 --> 00:18:20,240
Now, I'm just a businessman.

253
00:18:20,440 --> 00:18:21,680
I only care about profit.

254
00:18:22,720 --> 00:18:24,720
If anyone gets in the way of my money,

255
00:18:25,039 --> 00:18:26,559
then they're my enemy.

256
00:18:26,920 --> 00:18:28,279
What I want is simple.

257
00:18:28,519 --> 00:18:30,920
Delay the African Queen by six hours

258
00:18:30,920 --> 00:18:32,640
before it arrives at the Huatie base.

259
00:18:33,440 --> 00:18:34,319
When did you

260
00:18:34,559 --> 00:18:36,160
set your sights on Huatie?

261
00:18:36,519 --> 00:18:38,559
Railroads don't interest me.

262
00:18:38,920 --> 00:18:40,799
But Huatie's market cap...

263
00:18:41,160 --> 00:18:42,880
that I'm very interested in.

264
00:18:42,880 --> 00:18:43,640
Hades,

265
00:18:44,599 --> 00:18:45,680
let Anda go.

266
00:18:45,680 --> 00:18:46,680
Take me hostage instead.

267
00:18:47,519 --> 00:18:48,319
Wei Tian.

268
00:18:48,799 --> 00:18:50,960
We were once the best partners.

269
00:18:51,240 --> 00:18:52,640
Things ending up like this

270
00:18:52,680 --> 00:18:53,920
was never what I wanted.

271
00:18:54,000 --> 00:18:57,079
We're not partners anymore.

272
00:18:58,599 --> 00:18:59,599
To me,

273
00:19:00,279 --> 00:19:03,160
you're just a demon I want to take down.

274
00:19:03,160 --> 00:19:03,920
Wei Tian,

275
00:19:04,599 --> 00:19:06,079
let go of the past grudges.

276
00:19:06,319 --> 00:19:07,440
Let's work together

277
00:19:07,759 --> 00:19:09,640
and do something worthwhile.

278
00:19:09,880 --> 00:19:11,279
What's most worthwhile to me

279
00:19:12,480 --> 00:19:14,079
is putting a bullet in you.

280
00:19:14,640 --> 00:19:15,519
You're wrong.

281
00:19:16,240 --> 00:19:18,039
War is a soldier's true calling.

282
00:19:18,440 --> 00:19:19,839
I love war.

283
00:19:20,240 --> 00:19:21,839
In this world, places of war

284
00:19:21,839 --> 00:19:23,799
will always outnumber places of peace.

285
00:19:23,880 --> 00:19:24,680
Wei Tian,

286
00:19:24,839 --> 00:19:27,119
I despise your pointless sense of justice.

287
00:19:29,799 --> 00:19:31,200
I've stayed here all these years

288
00:19:32,000 --> 00:19:33,000
just waiting for you,

289
00:19:34,880 --> 00:19:36,240
waiting for you to show up.

290
00:19:37,440 --> 00:19:39,119
If I get even one chance

291
00:19:40,079 --> 00:19:41,119
to catch you,

292
00:19:41,599 --> 00:19:43,039
I will definitely kill you.

293
00:19:45,000 --> 00:19:45,960
In that case...

294
00:19:46,359 --> 00:19:49,359
Morris, tell them all to lower their guns.

295
00:19:50,880 --> 00:19:52,759
I want to see what he's got.

296
00:21:44,640 --> 00:21:45,079
Come on.

297
00:21:48,200 --> 00:21:48,680
Don't be afraid.

298
00:21:51,640 --> 00:21:52,440
Are you okay?

299
00:21:56,039 --> 00:21:57,759
I'm going to find Xiang Pingsheng and Marisa.

300
00:21:58,480 --> 00:21:59,759
Head to their construction base.

301
00:22:00,440 --> 00:22:02,039
Why not wait until daybreak?

302
00:22:02,079 --> 00:22:05,039
Hades will definitely keep attacking them.

303
00:22:05,319 --> 00:22:06,160
Because that way,

304
00:22:06,160 --> 00:22:08,079
they can manipulate Huatie's stock price.

305
00:22:12,559 --> 00:22:13,480
I'm leaving her to you.

306
00:22:13,480 --> 00:22:14,119
Okay.

307
00:22:14,599 --> 00:22:15,400
Wei Tian.

308
00:22:16,720 --> 00:22:17,559
Be careful.

309
00:22:18,720 --> 00:22:19,440
Don't worry.

310
00:22:23,920 --> 00:22:24,920
Are you okay?

311
00:22:25,400 --> 00:22:25,759
Let's go.

312
00:22:44,400 --> 00:22:45,720
They set off anyway.

313
00:22:45,920 --> 00:22:47,440
Until the stock market closes,

314
00:22:47,440 --> 00:22:48,440
we still have six hours.

315
00:22:48,440 --> 00:22:49,079
Prepare to move.

316
00:22:49,079 --> 00:22:49,680
Understood.

317
00:22:56,680 --> 00:22:57,920
Ready. Let's move.

318
00:23:28,400 --> 00:23:30,480
The last time we drove out on a mission together...

319
00:23:30,480 --> 00:23:31,720
how many years ago was that?

320
00:23:31,799 --> 00:23:33,000
A long time ago.

321
00:23:33,799 --> 00:23:36,000
What made you think of that all of a sudden?

322
00:23:36,920 --> 00:23:39,440
Can't help it. People get sentimental with age.

323
00:23:39,880 --> 00:23:40,599
That's normal.

324
00:23:43,599 --> 00:23:45,039
What do you think of Xiang Lai?

325
00:23:45,920 --> 00:23:46,720
He's pretty good.

326
00:23:47,640 --> 00:23:49,960
The kid doesn't easily get taken advantage of.

327
00:23:51,200 --> 00:23:52,519
Is that a compliment?

328
00:23:53,799 --> 00:23:55,359
Not getting taken advantage of is a good thing.

329
00:23:56,920 --> 00:23:58,039
He's a young man.

330
00:23:58,839 --> 00:24:00,559
A few bumps and bruises are normal.

331
00:24:46,640 --> 00:24:47,440
The power's out.

332
00:24:47,559 --> 00:24:48,480
Keep moving things.

333
00:24:48,559 --> 00:24:49,400
I'll go take a look.

334
00:24:49,400 --> 00:24:50,480
Probably tripped a breaker.

335
00:24:50,480 --> 00:24:50,880
Okay.

336
00:24:53,319 --> 00:24:54,119
Hurry up.

337
00:25:08,279 --> 00:25:09,640
The breaker didn't trip.

338
00:25:14,519 --> 00:25:15,440
Hands up!

339
00:25:16,680 --> 00:25:17,559
Put your hands up!

340
00:25:25,119 --> 00:25:27,599
Get out! Move!

341
00:25:40,319 --> 00:25:41,160
Take it out.

342
00:26:19,240 --> 00:26:20,400
Where's your boss?

343
00:26:20,400 --> 00:26:22,720
I don't know. Maybe he went to the construction site.

344
00:26:34,960 --> 00:26:36,720
You two, come with me.

345
00:26:49,559 --> 00:26:50,599
Take a good look!

346
00:26:50,599 --> 00:26:52,640
See what you get for helping the Chinese!

347
00:27:06,759 --> 00:27:07,880
I'm in position.

348
00:27:08,240 --> 00:27:09,240
Under this blazing sun,

349
00:27:09,240 --> 00:27:10,880
Captain, thanks for your hard work.

350
00:27:12,880 --> 00:27:15,759
Captain, Captain, can you hear me?

351
00:27:18,799 --> 00:27:21,200
Shalan, Shalan, calling Shalan.

352
00:27:21,839 --> 00:27:24,160
Shalan, can you hear me? Shalan.

353
00:27:26,279 --> 00:27:27,720
Calling Rossi, calling Rossi.

354
00:27:27,759 --> 00:27:29,319
Calling Wei Tian, calling Wei Tian.

355
00:27:44,839 --> 00:27:46,440
How come we didn't find a single cent?

356
00:27:48,880 --> 00:27:49,680
Let's go.

357
00:27:55,880 --> 00:27:56,319
Nothing.

358
00:28:02,759 --> 00:28:04,799
You guys are getting faster and faster.

359
00:28:20,440 --> 00:28:21,759
Just now, in the corner,

360
00:28:21,759 --> 00:28:23,240
we caught a few Chinese people.

361
00:28:23,240 --> 00:28:24,799
There shouldn't be anyone else.

362
00:28:25,839 --> 00:28:26,680
I told you

363
00:28:26,680 --> 00:28:28,680
there had to be Chinese people here.

364
00:28:37,160 --> 00:28:39,160
Now I'm giving you two choices.

365
00:28:39,440 --> 00:28:40,880
Either leave this place

366
00:28:41,079 --> 00:28:43,079
and keep paying us protection money,

367
00:28:43,559 --> 00:28:44,480
or stay right here,

368
00:28:44,480 --> 00:28:46,720
wait for your Chinese boss to get back,

369
00:28:47,000 --> 00:28:48,559
and die along with him.

370
00:29:21,920 --> 00:29:23,799
It shouldn't be this deserted right now.

371
00:29:26,880 --> 00:29:29,119
The signal is jammed. No service.

372
00:29:29,759 --> 00:29:31,720
Shalan, how's our signal?

373
00:29:34,599 --> 00:29:35,079
Mr. Xiang.

374
00:29:37,559 --> 00:29:39,240
The mobile signal is jammed here.

375
00:29:39,440 --> 00:29:41,039
Have someone scout the perimeter.

376
00:29:41,240 --> 00:29:41,599
Yes, sir.

377
00:29:42,400 --> 00:29:43,880
Looks like we're too late.

378
00:29:44,880 --> 00:29:46,920
It's unnervingly quiet.

379
00:29:53,920 --> 00:29:54,720
Help!

380
00:29:54,720 --> 00:29:55,480
They're back!

381
00:29:56,119 --> 00:29:57,920
Run! Take cover!

382
00:29:58,240 --> 00:30:00,160
Hide! Hurry!

383
00:30:01,000 --> 00:30:02,920
Help! Help!

384
00:30:03,960 --> 00:30:05,640
Chief, they're back!

385
00:30:10,880 --> 00:30:12,599
Quick! Quick!

386
00:30:18,799 --> 00:30:20,039
What are you doing here?

387
00:30:20,039 --> 00:30:20,960
Don't panic, everyone.

388
00:30:21,480 --> 00:30:23,079
We're here looking for someone.

389
00:30:23,160 --> 00:30:24,799
The person you're looking for isn't here.

390
00:30:24,799 --> 00:30:25,599
Leave!

391
00:30:26,240 --> 00:30:28,000
We mean no harm, alright?

392
00:30:28,559 --> 00:30:29,640
What happened here?

393
00:30:29,680 --> 00:30:31,200
Our people were captured.

394
00:30:31,880 --> 00:30:32,759
Who did this?

395
00:30:33,599 --> 00:30:35,920
Does this have to do with the railway?

396
00:30:36,079 --> 00:30:37,160
In the past, Sissoko

397
00:30:37,160 --> 00:30:38,759
abducted our people to work the mines.

398
00:30:39,079 --> 00:30:40,519
After the railway team arrived,

399
00:30:40,519 --> 00:30:41,720
our people were freed.

400
00:30:42,160 --> 00:30:43,559
They taught us knowledge

401
00:30:43,720 --> 00:30:45,079
and sent doctors to treat us.

402
00:30:45,160 --> 00:30:47,559
But Sissoko keeps sabotaging the railway,

403
00:30:47,559 --> 00:30:49,160
abducting and beating our children,

404
00:30:49,160 --> 00:30:51,000
and trafficking the girls from our tribe.

405
00:30:51,039 --> 00:30:52,279
They have guns,

406
00:30:52,319 --> 00:30:53,920
so there's nothing we can do

407
00:30:54,000 --> 00:30:55,359
but stay away from the Chinese.

408
00:31:00,079 --> 00:31:00,519
I understand.

409
00:31:02,240 --> 00:31:02,599
Thank you.

410
00:31:11,720 --> 00:31:12,519
Calling Captain.

411
00:31:14,319 --> 00:31:15,200
Shalan, Shalan.

412
00:31:15,559 --> 00:31:16,799
The signal dropped earlier.

413
00:31:17,160 --> 00:31:19,519
Shen Yu's signal is completely cut off.

414
00:31:20,039 --> 00:31:21,279
I know, I know. It's fine.

415
00:31:21,599 --> 00:31:23,440
I've connected to a backup frequency now.

416
00:31:23,559 --> 00:31:24,960
We can talk to each other.

417
00:31:25,480 --> 00:31:26,720
Understood. Copy that.

418
00:31:41,599 --> 00:31:42,359
Shalan,

419
00:31:42,359 --> 00:31:45,279
our power has been completely cut off.

420
00:32:03,039 --> 00:32:03,960
What's the situation?

421
00:32:04,039 --> 00:32:06,599
Site power is completely cut off.

422
00:32:06,599 --> 00:32:08,119
And Zhong An's comms

423
00:32:08,359 --> 00:32:09,480
have been jammed as well.

424
00:32:09,759 --> 00:32:10,559
What about yours?

425
00:32:10,680 --> 00:32:11,680
We can still get a signal.

426
00:32:12,279 --> 00:32:13,839
Because we're using high frequency.

427
00:32:16,680 --> 00:32:17,079
Mr. Xiang,

428
00:32:17,759 --> 00:32:18,519
the local residents

429
00:32:18,519 --> 00:32:19,799
have been enslaved by a militant

430
00:32:19,799 --> 00:32:20,559
named Sissoko.

431
00:32:20,799 --> 00:32:22,000
Ever since Huatie moved in,

432
00:32:22,000 --> 00:32:23,119
their influence has been disrupted.

433
00:32:23,359 --> 00:32:24,839
Now they're resorting to retaliation.

434
00:32:25,759 --> 00:32:27,440
Right now, I'm worried about the people at the base.

435
00:32:28,319 --> 00:32:29,400
Let's go. Start the car.

436
00:32:29,640 --> 00:32:30,400
Head to the base.

437
00:32:59,519 --> 00:33:00,039
I wonder

438
00:33:00,039 --> 00:33:02,119
how Madam Marisa is doing

439
00:33:02,160 --> 00:33:03,920
and when Wei Tian and the others will be back.

440
00:33:04,319 --> 00:33:06,039
With Wei Tian and my dad there, it'll be fine.

441
00:33:06,279 --> 00:33:07,400
We just need to wait patiently.

442
00:33:08,680 --> 00:33:10,359
About my kidnapping last time...

443
00:33:10,400 --> 00:33:12,039
I really owe it all to the two of you.

444
00:33:12,240 --> 00:33:13,000
You know what?

445
00:33:13,000 --> 00:33:14,640
Ever since you rescued me,

446
00:33:14,680 --> 00:33:16,640
I had this really long dream.

447
00:33:16,720 --> 00:33:18,599
I dreamed I was back home,

448
00:33:18,599 --> 00:33:20,119
eating my mom's cooking.

449
00:33:20,599 --> 00:33:24,640
Then I dreamed Wei Tian was doing the dishes,

450
00:33:25,279 --> 00:33:26,359
and I woke up.

451
00:33:28,440 --> 00:33:29,400
But seriously,

452
00:33:29,920 --> 00:33:31,880
do you want to move out of the Silent Protectors base?

453
00:33:32,160 --> 00:33:32,880
I just feel like

454
00:33:32,880 --> 00:33:34,039
if you keep staying

455
00:33:34,039 --> 00:33:34,960
over at their place,

456
00:33:35,039 --> 00:33:36,119
you'll be in danger again.

457
00:33:46,759 --> 00:33:47,599
All of you, over here!

458
00:33:48,359 --> 00:33:49,240
Erika got away!

459
00:33:49,319 --> 00:33:50,839
We have to catch that girl, hurry!

460
00:33:51,000 --> 00:33:52,039
You guys go this way.

461
00:33:52,079 --> 00:33:53,079
We must catch her!

462
00:33:53,160 --> 00:33:55,519
You guys go that way, hurry! Move!

463
00:34:03,319 --> 00:34:03,559
Hello.

464
00:34:03,559 --> 00:34:04,400
Hello, sir.

465
00:34:04,640 --> 00:34:05,559
What would you like to drink?

466
00:34:05,559 --> 00:34:05,960
Juice.

467
00:34:05,960 --> 00:34:06,319
Coffee.

468
00:34:06,319 --> 00:34:06,799
All right.

469
00:34:07,039 --> 00:34:07,480
Thank you.

470
00:34:08,519 --> 00:34:09,400
You know,

471
00:34:09,719 --> 00:34:10,800
when I first heard

472
00:34:10,800 --> 00:34:12,840
about being posted here,

473
00:34:13,440 --> 00:34:16,519
a lot of colleagues said it was backward

474
00:34:17,199 --> 00:34:19,440
and impoverished.

475
00:34:20,079 --> 00:34:21,159
But I've found

476
00:34:21,159 --> 00:34:23,559
the people here are quite genuine and warm.

477
00:34:41,880 --> 00:34:43,119
This way. You go over there.

478
00:34:52,760 --> 00:34:54,159
Let's go. We'll head back to the hotel first.

479
00:35:24,519 --> 00:35:24,880
Come on.

480
00:35:25,840 --> 00:35:26,840
It's safe here. Come on.

481
00:35:43,320 --> 00:35:43,880
Haibin.

482
00:35:45,199 --> 00:35:47,840
Um, do you have any lunch left?

483
00:35:47,840 --> 00:35:49,559
I haven't eaten. Can I have some?

484
00:35:49,920 --> 00:35:52,079
Miss An, today's your day off.

485
00:35:52,519 --> 00:35:54,480
Didn't Xiang Lai buy you lunch today?

486
00:35:56,559 --> 00:35:58,440
It wasn't as good as your cooking.

487
00:36:01,320 --> 00:36:02,079
Just give me some bread.

488
00:36:03,880 --> 00:36:05,519
Bread? Are you sure?

489
00:36:06,480 --> 00:36:08,480
Careful, you'll gain weight and never find a husband.

490
00:36:09,719 --> 00:36:12,480
I just want bread. Go get it, please!

491
00:36:13,320 --> 00:36:14,920
Fine, I'll get you a slice of bread.

492
00:36:14,920 --> 00:36:15,960
And two eggs.

493
00:36:16,400 --> 00:36:17,239
That's more like it.

494
00:36:17,239 --> 00:36:17,960
Wait here.

495
00:36:46,519 --> 00:36:47,159
Anyone here?

496
00:36:51,400 --> 00:36:52,199
Let's take a look inside.

497
00:37:16,920 --> 00:37:17,440
Come out.

498
00:37:18,880 --> 00:37:21,079
Don't kill me! Don't kill me!

499
00:37:23,159 --> 00:37:24,920
Don't kill me! Don't kill me!

500
00:37:25,880 --> 00:37:26,559
Don't kill me!

501
00:37:29,360 --> 00:37:30,800
You're with Huatie, right?

502
00:37:32,960 --> 00:37:33,519
I am.

503
00:37:34,320 --> 00:37:36,159
Put your hands down. Don't be afraid.

504
00:37:37,280 --> 00:37:39,360
I'm Xiang Pingsheng from Zhong An Security.

505
00:37:40,519 --> 00:37:41,679
What happened here?

506
00:37:44,880 --> 00:37:47,159
They just left. They were all armed.

507
00:37:47,920 --> 00:37:49,039
I heard gunshots,

508
00:37:49,199 --> 00:37:50,400
so I hid.

509
00:37:50,599 --> 00:37:51,519
Where's everyone else?

510
00:37:53,239 --> 00:37:54,079
I don't know.

511
00:37:57,039 --> 00:37:58,280
Who were they?

512
00:38:00,199 --> 00:38:01,159
I really don't know!

513
00:38:05,000 --> 00:38:06,400
Were they looking for something?

514
00:38:07,199 --> 00:38:08,639
I... I don't know.

515
00:38:08,719 --> 00:38:09,519
Stop asking.

516
00:38:09,719 --> 00:38:11,000
He probably doesn't know anything.

517
00:38:12,159 --> 00:38:14,639
All right, don't be scared.

518
00:38:25,519 --> 00:38:26,360
Let's go for a walk.

519
00:38:26,519 --> 00:38:27,960
Sure, let's look around.

520
00:38:30,000 --> 00:38:30,800
Captain.

521
00:38:31,599 --> 00:38:33,599
You stay here and protect them.

522
00:38:33,760 --> 00:38:35,400
If anything happens, contact Rossi.

523
00:38:35,400 --> 00:38:35,920
Understood.

524
00:41:03,199 --> 00:41:04,280
It's okay, it's okay.

525
00:41:14,880 --> 00:41:15,559
Got a minute?

526
00:41:25,599 --> 00:41:26,559
Who is she, anyway?

527
00:41:26,719 --> 00:41:27,679
Didn't get a chance to ask.

528
00:41:34,719 --> 00:41:35,119
Here.

529
00:41:51,039 --> 00:41:52,440
Why were those people chasing you?

530
00:41:57,280 --> 00:41:58,159
Don't worry.

531
00:41:59,119 --> 00:42:00,800
This hotel is run by Chinese people.

532
00:42:01,079 --> 00:42:01,800
It's very safe.

533
00:42:07,119 --> 00:42:08,480
So what actually happened?

534
00:42:09,079 --> 00:42:09,920
Silent Protectors.

535
00:42:12,320 --> 00:42:13,119
Silent Protectors.

536
00:42:13,760 --> 00:42:16,280
Silent Protectors? Why are you looking for them?

537
00:42:16,280 --> 00:42:17,400
What's your name?

538
00:42:18,559 --> 00:42:19,800
My name is Erika.

539
00:42:19,920 --> 00:42:22,199
I need the Silent Protectors to save my sisters.

540
00:42:23,480 --> 00:42:24,840
What happened to your sisters?

541
00:42:25,679 --> 00:42:28,159
Our tribe is controlled by Sissoko.

542
00:42:28,440 --> 00:42:30,119
They took the girls from our tribe...

543
00:42:30,119 --> 00:42:32,360
...and locked them away in terrible places.

544
00:42:32,480 --> 00:42:34,840
Only the Silent Protectors can save them.

545
00:42:36,440 --> 00:42:38,679
So you escaped on your own?

546
00:42:44,280 --> 00:42:46,719
I never thought it would be wrecked like this.

547
00:42:47,199 --> 00:42:49,119
To seize the advanced equipment,

548
00:42:49,480 --> 00:42:51,480
they used crude and brutal destruction.

549
00:43:01,880 --> 00:43:03,880
President Xiang, Mr. Wei.

550
00:43:04,719 --> 00:43:06,519
Three workers from the base are missing.

551
00:43:06,760 --> 00:43:08,519
They were likely kidnapped by militants.

552
00:43:10,360 --> 00:43:11,280
Take a few men

553
00:43:11,360 --> 00:43:13,119
and sweep the perimeter of the base first.

554
00:43:13,320 --> 00:43:14,840
See if there's anyone suspicious.

555
00:43:14,840 --> 00:43:15,320
Yes, sir.

556
00:43:31,559 --> 00:43:34,519
That look of fear... I like it.
